# Cloudflare DNS safety

## Gate

Load on every authorized Cloudflare DNS turn (inventory or mutate). Skip when
the turn never touches Cloudflare DNS.

## Read-only default

These are fine without an extra destructive verb when Cloudflare DNS is
authorized:

- `list_dns_records`
- `get_dns_record`

Do **not** call `create_dns_record`, `update_dns_record`, or
`delete_dns_record` unless the user gave an explicit verb **this turn**
naming the record (FQDN and type, or record id).

## Mutate gates (explicit verb required)

| Risk | Needs this turn | MCP |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Delete record | **delete** / **remove** + name/type or recordId | `delete_dns_record` |
| Create record | **create** / **add** + type + name + content | `create_dns_record` |
| Update record | **update** / **point** / **change** + name/type + new content | `update_dns_record` |
| Bulk / “point everything at X” | **all** / **every** / named list of FQDNs — not a guess | per-record tools only; no zone replace |
| Apex / MX / mail TXT | named FQDN + values + acknowledgment of blast radius | create/update/delete as asked |

Ambiguous “clean up DNS” → ask once for names/types; do not mass-delete.

## Prefer update-in-place

Prefer `update_dns_record` over delete+create. Delete+create only when the
user asked to replace or type cannot be updated in place — state why.

## Refuse

- Pasting Cloudflare API tokens, global keys, or Origin CA keys into chat
- Inventing `recordId` or zone ids
- Replacing an entire zone from a guessed desired state
- Touching non-DNS Cloudflare products under this plugin
- Inventing MCP tool names beyond the live `user-mcp_cloudflare` map

## Irreversible

If the ask would remove production traffic or mail records and the user did
not name them, **stop** and state the risk in one sentence — do not guess.

## Receipt examples (safe)

Inventory: `list_dns_records` name `app.example.com` → `A`
`203.0.113.10`, proxied true, id `abc…` — no mutate.

Authorized point: update id `abc…` content → `203.0.113.20`; receipt FQDN +
type + content + proxied — no tokens.

